candidates.definition:
**RemNi:** a generic definition (AGI can perform any intellectual task a human can). It resolves YES if such a system is 'created and publicly announced' before 1 January of the year. On the 2030 market, a moderator edit (2025-11-02) makes Manifold's 'In what specific year will we hit AGI?' the baseline. That edit is not in the 2040 market's text.

**Metaculus 5121** requires a single unified system that can:
- reliably pass a 2-hour adversarial Turing test (text, images, audio);
- robotically assemble a circa-2021 Ferrari 312 T4 1:8 scale model;
- score at least 90% mean accuracy on the Hendrycks Q&A dataset;
- reach at least 90% top-1 strict accuracy on APPS interview-level problems.

It resolves by direct demonstration, a credible developer statement, or a majority vote of a committee (the question author plus two AI experts).

YES if before 2029 Congress enacts federal legislation with a projected net cost of at least $500B (CBO, OMB or broadly accepted estimates), and:
- its law text, section titles, congressional findings, or White House / Cabinet-level fact sheets explicitly describe it as responding to unemployment or displacement caused by or strongly linked to AI or automation;
- a majority of the cost goes to cash or income support, unemployment insurance or wage support, retraining, or similar worker-focused measures.
